// EXPECT: PASS
// Cluster F over-rejection guard, second axis. `b.act(x)` where `act` is a CLOSURE STORED IN A FIELD
// is NOT a method call, even though it parses to the same `Expr::CallExpr { callee: FieldAccess }`
// node the new capability inheritance hooks into. It must keep going through the existing
// `field_closures` descent (which walks the real lambda body) and must not be spuriously charged.
//
// KNOWN CONFLATION, deliberately NOT exercised here: if the field name COLLIDES with an impl method
// name, the program is already rejected before reaching the capability lane —
// `ANUBIS_ARITY_MISMATCH: method `f` expects 0 argument(s), got 1` — because method arity checking is
// keyed by bare name with no receiver-type resolution. That reject predates this fix (verified
// against the pre-fix binary). It means the collision case is currently moot, but if the arity check
// is ever made receiver-aware, the bare-name capability lookup would become a live false reject on
// that shape. Recorded so the dependency is not rediscovered the hard way.
struct Holder { act: i64 }
fn main() {
    let b = Holder { act: |x| x + 1 };
    print(b.act(41));
}
